        {
          "ruleId": "pmat/pinned-instrument-mcp-index-stats-deletes-a-cli-built-index",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "pmat 3.41.1 - the version this PR pins on every fleet runner - deletes its own index when its MCP server is asked about it. Measured in this worktree, twice, deterministically: `pmat query \"x\" --rebuild-index --limit 1` (CLI) writes .pmat/context.idx/manifest.json at 18:40:59 and .pmat/context.db at 18:41:01; the MCP tool `pmat_index_stats` (server `pmat --mode mcp`, pid 2468072, the one attached to this session) then answers 'Internal error: the index is stale: .../.pmat/context.db was written after .../.pmat/context.idx/manifest.json, so the manifest does not describe the database', and `ls -la .pmat/` afterwards shows only .gitignore - context.db (522 MB) and context.idx/ are gone. Reproduced 2/2. The same index survives, 7/7, every CLI path exercised here: pmat query with and without --rebuild-index, pmat analyze satd/tdg/complexity, scripts/check_baseline_ratchets.sh, scripts/check_complexity_ratchet.sh, scripts/check_tool_versions.sh and scripts/pr_review_duplication_scan.sh. The first loss of this review's index (built 18:27, absent by 18:29 when `pmat comply check --checks CB-200` printed 'no index in .') was not bisected to a trigger and is consistent with, not proven to be, the same mechanism. NOT a regression claim: pmat 3.40.1 was not tested on this box, so whether this is new in 3.41.x is not known."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "tools.toml"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 56
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "measured",
            "command": [
