            ],
            "corroborating_results": {
              "mcp_error": "the index is stale: context.db was written after context.idx/manifest.json",
              "context_db_mtime": "2026-09-18 18:41:01.522 +0200",
              "manifest_mtime": "2026-09-18 18:40:59.408 +0200",
              "reproductions": "2/2",
              "cli_paths_that_leave_the_index_intact": "7/7"
            },
            "failure_scenario": "Any agent session with the pmat MCP server attached (this one had it, as does every Claude Code session on this box - nine `pmat --mode mcp` processes were live) loses .pmat/context.db on its first pmat_index_stats call. `pmat comply check --checks CB-200` then reports 'no index in .' and builds a private cache index (105 s here) - CB-200 stays MEASURED through the #1008 fallback, which is why this PR's 599 and this review's 599 agree - but `pmat query` needs a 95 s rebuild, and scripts/dogfood.sh:1004 reads 'no .pmat/context.db' as CB-200 UNMEASURED and marks pmat-comply FAIL. A dogfood run started between an MCP stats call and the next rebuild fails on the instrument, not the tree, and the operator reads it as debt. This is a pmat defect to file upstream against 3.41.1, not something this PR can fix; it is recorded here because this PR is what makes 3.41.1 the instrument on every runner."
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "pmat/required-check-workspace-test-is-red-on-this-head-runner-killed-the-container",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "On the reviewed head 0fd8deb79, the required check `workspace-test` (CI run 35366983482, job 105673963954, runner yoga-build2) is FAILURE with exit code 143: the job log ends '/home/noah/eph-build2/_work/_temp/....sh: line 36: 27323 Killed  docker run --rm ...' at 16:26:36Z, 4 m 24 s in, while the preceding 60 lines are rustc warnings from compiling aprender-profile's sprint50_validate_tests - no test binary ran and no test result exists. The diff changes zero .rs files and zero Cargo.toml files (`git diff --name-only | grep -cE '(^|/)(Cargo\\\\.toml|src/|crates/)'` = 0, exit 1), so the compile it interrupted is not this PR's code. The other red check, `present` (pr-review-quorum, job 105671714910), fails with 'the head carries no evidence/pr-review/3491' - the receipt this review commits is the fix, so it is not a finding."
          },
